module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.NonvanishingSpelling.Trivialize
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionProduct.Basic
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Ratios of a generating family of global sections of an invertible module

Let `X` be a scheme, `L` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module and `(sᵢ)` a family of global sections of
`L`. On the nonvanishing open `X_{sᵢ}` the section `sᵢ` is a basis of `L` — that is the
trivialization clause of Stacks Tag 01CY, stated as
`Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.existsUnique_smul_eq` — so every `s_k` is a *unique* multiple of
`sᵢ` there. This file defines that multiple, the ratio `s_k / sᵢ`, and proves:

* the ratio out of `sᵢ` of `sᵢ` itself is `1`, hence the ratios out of `sᵢ` **span the unit
  ideal** of `Γ(X, X_{sᵢ})` (`span_range_ratio`);
* on an overlap the ratios satisfy the **cocycle identity** `s_k/sᵢ = (sⱼ/sᵢ) · (s_k/sⱼ)`
  (`ratio_cocycle`), so the family of ratios out of `sᵢ` and the family out of `sⱼ` differ by the
  single factor `sⱼ/sᵢ`;
* that factor is a **unit** on the overlap (`transUnit`, `isUnit_resO_ratio`), its inverse being
  `sᵢ/sⱼ`, which is the case `k = i` of the cocycle identity.

These are the data glued in Stacks Tag 01NE.

## The generation hypothesis

Tag 01NE's hypothesis is that the `sᵢ` *generate* `L`. For a sheaf of modules on a space that is
a stalkwise condition, and it is stated here as `GeneratesStalks`: every element of every stalk
`Lₓ` is an `𝒪_{X,x}`-combination of the germs of the `sᵢ`. By
`isOpenCover_nvCover_of_generatesStalks`, it implies that the nonvanishing opens cover `X`: if
every germ `sᵢ` lay in `𝔪ₓ · Lₓ` then so would every combination of them, hence all of `Lₓ`, and
`Stacks.SectionProduct.exists_notMem_maximalSmul` says it does not.

The converse also holds: on `X_{sᵢ}` the section `sᵢ` is a basis, so a point of `X_{sᵢ}` has its
whole stalk generated by `germ sᵢ` alone
(`Stacks.SectionProduct.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff_generates`).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.div`: the ratio `t / s` of a section of `L` by a nonvanishing
  global one, over any open inside the nonvanishing locus.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.nvOpen`, `nvCover`: `X_s`, and the family `i ↦ X_{sᵢ}`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.ratio`: **the ratio `s_k / sᵢ`** over `X_{sᵢ}`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.transUnit`: **the transition factor `sⱼ/sᵢ` as a unit** of
  `Γ(X, W)` for any `W` inside both nonvanishing opens.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.GeneratesStalks`: the `sᵢ` generate `L`, stalkwise.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.ratio_smul` and `resO_ratio_smul`: the defining property
  `(s_k/sᵢ) · sᵢ = s_k`, over `X_{sᵢ}` and over any open inside it.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.ratio_self`, `span_range_ratio`: `sᵢ/sᵢ = 1`, hence the ratios
  out of `sᵢ` span the unit ideal.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.ratio_cocycle`: **the cocycle identity.**
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.isUnit_resO_ratio`: **the transition factor is a unit.**
* `Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections.isOpenCover_nvCover_of_generatesStalks`: **a generating family's
  nonvanishing opens cover `X`.**

## Implementation notes

`div` is defined by choice from `Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.existsUnique_smul_eq`, and every
identity between ratios follows from injectivity of multiplication by `sᵢ`
(`eq_of_smul_eq_smul`): both sides multiply `sᵢ` to the same section.

`resM`, `resO` and `resT` are the restrictions of a section of `L`, of a section of `𝒪_X`, and of
a global section of `L`, in terms of which restriction is semilinear:
`resM h (a • u) = resO h a • resM h u` (`resM_smul`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.ModuleStalk

universe u

namespace Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} {L : X.Modules}

/-- Restriction of a section of an `𝒪_X`-module to a smaller open. -/
abbrev resM {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W) (u : Γ(L, W)) : Γ(L, W') :=
  L.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op u

/-- Restriction of a section of the structure sheaf to a smaller open. -/
abbrev resO {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W) (a : Γ(X, W)) : Γ(X, W') :=
  X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op a

/-- Restriction of a global section of an `𝒪_X`-module. -/
abbrev resT (W : X.Opens) (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) : Γ(L, W) := resM (le_top : W ≤ ⊤) s

/-- **Restriction is semilinear**: restricting a scalar multiple multiplies by the restricted
scalar. -/
theorem resM_smul {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W) (a : Γ(X, W)) (u : Γ(L, W)) :
    resM h (a • u) = resO h a • resM h u :=
  L.val.map_smul (homOfLE h).op a u

/-- Restricting the restriction of a global section is its restriction to the smaller open. -/
theorem resM_resT {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W) (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) :
    resM h (resT W s) = resT W' s := by
  simp only [resM, resT, ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp]
  rfl

/-- Restriction of sections of the structure sheaf is a ring map: the unit. -/
theorem resO_one {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W) : resO h (1 : Γ(X, W)) = 1 := map_one _

/-- Restriction of sections of the structure sheaf is a ring map: products. -/
theorem resO_mul {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W) (a b : Γ(X, W)) :
    resO h (a * b) = resO h a * resO h b := map_mul _ _ _

/-! ### Division by a nonvanishing section -/

variable [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- `X_s`, the nonvanishing open of a global section. -/
abbrev nvOpen (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) : X.Opens :=
  Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.nonvanishingOpen X L s

/-- **Multiplication by a nonvanishing section is injective** on any open inside its
nonvanishing locus. -/
theorem smul_injective (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) {W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ nvOpen L s) :
    Function.Injective fun a : Γ(X, W) => a • resT W s :=
  (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.bijective_smul X L s hW).injective

/-- Two sections of `𝒪_X` that multiply a nonvanishing `s` to the same section are equal. -/
theorem eq_of_smul_eq_smul (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) {W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ nvOpen L s) {a b : Γ(X, W)}
    (h : a • resT W s = b • resT W s) : a = b :=
  smul_injective s hW h

/-- The ratio `t / s` of a section of `L` by a nonvanishing one. -/
def div (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) {W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ nvOpen L s) (t : Γ(L, W)) : Γ(X, W) :=
  (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.existsUnique_smul_eq X L s hW t).choose

/-- The defining property of the ratio: `(t/s) · s = t`. -/
@[simp] theorem div_smul (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) {W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ nvOpen L s) (t : Γ(L, W)) :
    div s hW t • resT W s = t :=
  (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.existsUnique_smul_eq X L s hW t).choose_spec.1

/-- The ratio is the *only* section multiplying `s` to `t`. -/
theorem eq_div (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) {W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ nvOpen L s) {t : Γ(L, W)} {a : Γ(X, W)}
    (h : a • resT W s = t) : a = div s hW t :=
  (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.existsUnique_smul_eq X L s hW t).choose_spec.2 a h

/-! ### The ratios of a family of global sections -/

variable {ι : Type*}

/-- The `i`-th nonvanishing open of a family of global sections. -/
abbrev nvCover (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (i : ι) : X.Opens := nvOpen L (s i)

/-- The ratio `sₖ / sᵢ`, a section of `𝒪_X` over the nonvanishing open of `sᵢ`. -/
def ratio (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (i k : ι) : Γ(X, nvCover s i) :=
  div (s i) le_rfl (resT (nvCover s i) (s k))

/-- **The defining property of the ratio** `(s_k/sᵢ) · sᵢ = s_k`, over `X_{sᵢ}`. -/
theorem ratio_smul (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (i k : ι) :
    ratio s i k • resT (nvCover s i) (s i) = resT (nvCover s i) (s k) :=
  div_smul _ _ _

/-- The ratio on any open inside the nonvanishing open of `sᵢ`. -/
theorem resO_ratio_smul (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) {i : ι} {W : X.Opens} (hi : W ≤ nvCover s i) (k : ι) :
    resO hi (ratio s i k) • resT W (s i) = resT W (s k) := by
  have h := congrArg (resM hi) (ratio_smul s i k)
  rwa [resM_smul, resM_resT, resM_resT] at h

/-- The ratio of `sᵢ` by itself is `1`. -/
@[simp] theorem ratio_self (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (i : ι) : ratio s i i = 1 :=
  (eq_div (s i) le_rfl (one_smul _ _)).symm

/-- **The cocycle identity** `sₖ/sᵢ = (sⱼ/sᵢ) · (sₖ/sⱼ)`, on any open on which both `sᵢ` and
`sⱼ` are nonvanishing. -/
theorem ratio_cocycle (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) {i j : ι} {W : X.Opens} (hi : W ≤ nvCover s i)
    (hj : W ≤ nvCover s j) (k : ι) :
    resO hi (ratio s i k) = resO hi (ratio s i j) * resO hj (ratio s j k) := by
  refine eq_of_smul_eq_smul (s i) hi ?_
  rw [resO_ratio_smul s hi k, mul_comm, mul_smul, resO_ratio_smul s hi j, resO_ratio_smul s hj k]

/-- `(sⱼ/sᵢ) · (sᵢ/sⱼ) = 1` on the overlap: the case `k = i` of the cocycle identity. -/
theorem resO_ratio_mul_resO_ratio (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) {i j : ι} {W : X.Opens}
    (hi : W ≤ nvCover s i) (hj : W ≤ nvCover s j) :
    resO hi (ratio s i j) * resO hj (ratio s j i) = 1 := by
  rw [← ratio_cocycle s hi hj i, ratio_self, resO_one]

/-- **The transition ratio `sⱼ/sᵢ` as a unit on the overlap**, its inverse being `sᵢ/sⱼ`. -/
def transUnit (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) {i j : ι} {W : X.Opens} (hi : W ≤ nvCover s i)
    (hj : W ≤ nvCover s j) : Γ(X, W)ˣ where
  val := resO hi (ratio s i j)
  inv := resO hj (ratio s j i)
  val_inv := resO_ratio_mul_resO_ratio s hi hj
  inv_val := by
    rw [mul_comm]; exact resO_ratio_mul_resO_ratio s hi hj

/-- The underlying section of `transUnit` is the restriction of the ratio `sⱼ/sᵢ`. -/
@[simp] theorem transUnit_val (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) {i j : ι} {W : X.Opens} (hi : W ≤ nvCover s i)
    (hj : W ≤ nvCover s j) : (transUnit s hi hj : Γ(X, W)) = resO hi (ratio s i j) := rfl

/-- **The transition ratio is a unit on the overlap.** -/
theorem isUnit_resO_ratio (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) {i j : ι} {W : X.Opens} (hi : W ≤ nvCover s i)
    (hj : W ≤ nvCover s j) : IsUnit (resO hi (ratio s i j)) :=
  ⟨transUnit s hi hj, rfl⟩

/-- The ratios out of `sᵢ` span the unit ideal, because `sᵢ / sᵢ = 1`. -/
theorem span_range_ratio (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (i : ι) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range (ratio s i)) = ⊤ := by
  rw [Ideal.eq_top_iff_one, ← ratio_self s i]
  exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-! ### Generation and the nonvanishing cover -/

/-- **A family of global sections generates `L`**, stalkwise: the germs of the `sᵢ` generate
every stalk of `L` over the corresponding stalk of `𝒪_X`. For a sheaf of modules on a space,
surjectivity of the associated morphism out of the free module is exactly this condition at every
point, so this is the stalkwise reading of "the `sᵢ` generate `L`". -/
@[ega "0 5.1.1", sga "6 II 2.1.1" "special case"]
def GeneratesStalks (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (x : X) (w : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.presheaf x),
    ∃ (t : Finset ι) (r : ι → X.presheaf.stalk x),
      w = ∑ i ∈ t, r i • (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s i)

/-- **A generating family does not vanish simultaneously at any point.** If all the germs lay in
`𝔪ₓ · Lₓ` then so would every element of `Lₓ`, and the basis germ of a trivialization through `x`
does not. -/
theorem exists_mem_nvCover_of_generatesStalks (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (hs : GeneratesStalks s) (x : X) :
    ∃ i, x ∈ nvCover s i := by
  by_contra hx
  simp only [not_exists] at hx
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := Stacks.SectionProduct.exists_notMem_maximalSmul L x
  obtain ⟨t, r, hwr⟩ := hs x w
  refine hw (hwr ▸ Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ?_)
  have hi := hx i
  rw [Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.mem_nonvanishingOpen, Stacks.Ample.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff,
    not_not] at hi
  exact hi

/-- **The nonvanishing opens of a generating family cover `X`.** -/
theorem isOpenCover_nvCover_of_generatesStalks (s : ι → Γ(L, ⊤)) (hs : GeneratesStalks s) :
    IsOpenCover (nvCover s) := by
  refine eq_top_iff.2 fun x _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_mem_nvCover_of_generatesStalks s hs x
  exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨i, hi⟩

end Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections

end
